      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.3,
          "end": 4.93,
          "en": "I mentioned one other modern feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.93,
          "end": 6.97,
          "en": "which we can use a node now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.97,
          "end": 9.23,
          "en": "which I didn't use throughout this entire course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.23,
          "end": 12.61,
          "en": "And that would be promises in core APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.61,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "And that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 16.22,
          "en": "I did use promises throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.22,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "we have whole modules dedicated to promises and async await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "So you absolutely should know what promises are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 26.93,
          "en": "how they work and why we use them by now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.93,
          "end": 30,
          "en": "We use them because a lot of third party libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30,
          "end": 34.09,
          "en": "and also our own code can of course utilize promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.09,
          "end": 38.22,
          "en": "to handle potentially asynchronous operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.22,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "Now there is one part of the node apps we wrote thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 44.61,
          "en": "which doesn't really leverage promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 48.28,
          "en": "and that would be the core APIs baked into node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.28,
          "end": 50.87,
          "en": "I'm talking about things like read file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.87,
          "end": 53.24,
          "en": "from the file system module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.24,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "There we use this callback based approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "And the reason for that is very simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 61.19,
          "en": "when Node.js was created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.19,
          "end": 63.76,
          "en": "promises simply weren't a thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.76,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "they didn't land in mainstream JavaScript yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 72.08,
          "en": "that's why Node.js and its core APIs are callback based.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.52,
          "end": 74.94,
          "en": "Now, of course, here, we're using a different approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.94,
          "end": 76.93,
          "en": "of sending the file back anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.93,
          "end": 79.58,
          "en": "But if we switch back to the previous approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.58,
          "end": 81.43,
          "en": "and if you had some operation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.43,
          "end": 84.01,
          "en": "that needs to read a file or do anything else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.01,
          "end": 86.21000000000001,
          "en": "with a core node module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.21000000000001,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "you might wish to be able to use a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 90.98,
          "en": "instead of this callback approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.98,
          "end": 93.61,
          "en": "which you're forced to use unfortunately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.61,
          "end": 95.33,
          "en": "while there are good news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.33,
          "end": 98.28,
          "en": "a lot of core APIs baked into node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.28,
          "end": 101.543,
          "en": "now also have promise support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.46000000000001,
          "end": 104.89,
          "en": "Again, we can dive into the official docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.89,
          "end": 108.00999999999999,
          "en": "and there if you check out the file system documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.00999999999999,
          "end": 110.87,
          "en": "we'll find one interesting thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.87,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "Data we find all the methods we can use on the file system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 115.75,
          "en": "that's all nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.75,
          "end": 118.90299999999999,
          "en": "but if we scroll down further,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.01,
          "end": 124.42,
          "en": "we see that there is a fs Promises API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.42,
          "end": 128.02,
          "en": "And essentially, that's all the file system features here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.02,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "now available in a promise based version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 135.41,
          "en": "So for example, we also have a write file method now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.41,
          "end": 138.65,
          "en": "which actually embraces promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.65,
          "end": 141.73,
          "en": "so that we can use promises with these core APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.73,
          "end": 144.14,
          "en": "And a lot of the built in core APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.14,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "have such a promise version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 148.32999999999998,
          "en": "How do we use that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.32999999999998,
          "end": 150.17000000000002,
          "en": "Well, we need to import the file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.67000000000002,
          "en": "slightly differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.67000000000002,
          "end": 156.67000000000002,
          "en": "Instead of from fs, we import from fs/promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.01,
          "end": 159.16,
          "en": "And that's all, if you by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.16,
          "end": 164.02,
          "en": "use the old D require import syntax, it's the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.02,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "So there you can also use promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 168.8,
          "en": "even if you're not using the other import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.8,
          "end": 169.94,
          "en": "I showed you here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.94,
          "end": 171.8,
          "en": "Actually, I have to step in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.8,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "This is not correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 176.07999999999998,
          "en": "You would import it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.07999999999998,
          "end": 178.02,
          "en": "if you use the other import syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 180.35,
          "en": "You access the promises proper key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.35,
          "end": 182.74,
          "en": "on the imported file system object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.74,
          "end": 184.85,
          "en": "And this promises property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 184.85,
          "end": 187.05,
          "en": "exposes the file system object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 187.05,
          "end": 190.9,
          "en": "with all those file system methods using promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 190.9,
          "end": 193.47,
          "en": "This is the proper way of importing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 195.91,
          "en": "Now, since we use the different import syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.91,
          "end": 198.57,
          "en": "I unfortunately wrote this incorrect syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.57,
          "end": 201.67000000000002,
          "en": "Keep in mind if you would use that upper import syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 201.67000000000002,
          "end": 203.29,
          "en": "it's this year,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 203.29,
          "end": 204.57,
          "en": "this is how you would get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 209.24,
          "en": "to those promise based API's not this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 209.24,
          "end": 210.37,
          "en": "Just a little addition here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 210.37,
          "end": 213.13,
          "en": "which I recognized after I recorded this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 213.13,
          "end": 214.93,
          "en": "Sorry for the inconvenience here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 214.93,
          "end": 216.05,
          "en": "In this module of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.05,
          "end": 218.363,
          "en": "we're using this syntax anyways though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.85,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "Now with that, we got the file system object available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 225.57999999999998,
          "en": "And we can call read file on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.57999999999998,
          "end": 229.38,
          "en": "but this read file method now returns a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 234.07999999999998,
          "en": "which eventually will resolve to the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 234.07999999999998,
          "end": 236.78,
          "en": "where to the err or data we're getting back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 236.78,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "So now we can grab this call back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "and remove it from here and remove that third argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 245.34,
          "en": "And instead use then and catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 245.34,
          "end": 247.84,
          "en": "or async await whatever you prefer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 247.84,
          "end": 250.55,
          "en": "just as you learned it throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.55,
          "end": 252.23,
          "en": "And that's of course pretty nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 252.23,
          "end": 255.49,
          "en": "because now we can use all the promise advantages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 255.49,
          "end": 258.69,
          "en": "like promise chaining to escape callback hell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 262.01,
          "en": "on core APIs like this one as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 262.01,
          "end": 263.9,
          "en": "One adjustment we need to make though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 263.9,
          "end": 265.63,
          "en": "now since we're using promises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.63,
          "end": 268.65,
          "en": "of course in the ven method, we never get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.65,
          "end": 270.47,
          "en": "here we just get the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 270.47,
          "end": 272.44,
          "en": "If we would want to handle errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 272.44,
          "end": 274.38,
          "en": "we would have to add a catch method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 274.38,
          "end": 277.06,
          "en": "and then here we can handle any error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 277.06,
          "end": 279.74,
          "en": "we might get when we try to reach that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 279.74,
          "end": 282.97,
          "en": "So that is how we could transform this code to promises now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 282.97,
          "end": 285.953,
          "en": "and they offer if we now start this server here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 286.8,
          "end": 289.19,
          "en": "We again see our file being served here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 289.19,
          "end": 291.06,
          "en": "we see our page being loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 293.05,
          "en": "but now with the promise based version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 293.05,
          "end": 295.78,
          "en": "of this core node module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 295.78,
          "end": 300.33,
          "en": "Now just as the new import syntax, it's 100% optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 300.33,
          "end": 302.55,
          "en": "It's not better than the average approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 302.55,
          "end": 304.31,
          "en": "you might simply prefer it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 304.31,
          "end": 306.51,
          "en": "because you might prefer promises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 306.51,
          "end": 310,
          "en": "especially if you chain multiple promises for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 310,
          "end": 312.58,
          "en": "And therefore this is definitely all the feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 312.58,
